<h1>Week 20</h1>

<p><strong>From:</strong> Lana</p>
<p><strong>Artist:</strong> X</p>
<p><strong>Album:</strong> <em>Los Angeles</em></p>

<p>Kayla,</p>

<p>
This week I give you <em>Los Angeles</em> by X.
</p>

<p>
Such a great album. I would love to meet Exene. I can’t help but wonder what it was like being a woman in a male-dominated genre.
</p>

<p>
“Los Angeles” was the reason to buy the album, but there are some really good gems on this one too. “Soul Kitchen,” “Your Phone’s Off the Hook, But You’re Not,” “Nausea,” and “The Unheard Music” are my favorites.
</p>

<p>
I used to like “Johnny Hit and Run Paulene” too, and that one got a lot of airplay on punk stations. But I think it’s about rape, though I’m not completely sure.
</p>

<p>
Exene’s voice is so distinct and original, kind of like how Kate Pierson from the B-52’s is immediately recognizable.
</p>

<p>
This album reminds me of Lisa and the fun I had in my early 20s.
</p>

<p>
I saw them live, and I remember being a tiny bit afraid because the guys who were slam dancing were punching people in the face. So we stood farther back. But they sounded so good live.
</p>

<p>
I hope you enjoy this one.
</p>

<p>
I love you so much!!
</p>

<p>
Thanks for spending a Rosita’s day with me. 🌮❤️🌮
</p>

<p>
Mom
</p>

